{"content":[{"c":["SHIMEA"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Alternate name for Shammah, Jesse’s third son, in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.13","r":"1Chr.2.13","rawR":"1Chr.2.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.13","value":"1Chr.2.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 2:13"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.20.7","r":"1Chr.20.7","rawR":"1Chr.20.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.20.7","value":"1Chr.20.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"20:7"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Shammah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Shammah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Shammah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Shammah #2"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. David’s son borne to him by Bathsheba during his reign in Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.3.5","r":"1Chr.3.5","rawR":"1Chr.3.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.3.5","value":"1Chr.3.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 3:5"},"). He is called Shammua in ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.5.14","r":"2Sam.5.14","rawR":"2Sam.5.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.5.14","value":"2Sam.5.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Samuel 5:14"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.14.4","r":"1Chr.14.4","rawR":"1Chr.14.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.14.4","value":"1Chr.14.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 14:4"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Uzzah’s son, the father of Haggiah and a descendant of Levi through Merari’s line (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.30","r":"1Chr.6.30","rawR":"1Chr.6.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.30","value":"1Chr.6.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:30"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Gershonite Levite, Michael’s son, the father of Berekiah, and the grandfather of Asaph. Asaph, with Heman and Ethan, was appointed by David to lead the musicians before the sanctuary (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.39","r":"1Chr.6.39","rawR":"1Chr.6.39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.39","value":"1Chr.6.39"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:39"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Shimea","provenance":